// Monster spawn table for the linear-floor world (town → forest 1..MAX_FLOOR).
//
// Each entry tells `VoronoiSpawner` which monsters / packs are eligible
// on a given floor. The spawner picks one entry per chosen Voronoi cell
// at build time. See docs/design/SPAWNING.md for the algorithm and
// docs/design/ENEMIES.md for the per-monster identity / mechanic.
//
// **Currently active roster:** Giant Rat only, as the first step of the
// forest content pass. The legacy 26-floor dungeon spawn table from the
// previous milestone is preserved at the bottom of this file (commented
// out) so we can lift entries back in as we wire up new monsters.
//
// Schema reminder:
//   (monster: "Name", min_floor: i32, max_floor: i32, min_group: u32,
//    max_group: u32, flee_threshold: f32, spawn_on_liquid: bool)
//   (group: [(monster, min_count, max_count), ...], min_floor, max_floor, flee_threshold)
(
  spawns: [
    // ====================================================================
    // FOREST — active spawns
    // ====================================================================

    // Giant Rat: introductory swarm threat on both forest floors.
    // Pack size 1–3 keeps Forest 1 light; the Voronoi spawner caps total
    // packs per floor at `BUDGET_BASE + depth` (3 on floor 1, 4 on floor 2).
    (monster: "Giant Rat", min_floor: 1, max_floor: 2, min_group: 1, max_group: 3),

    // Jackal: paired with rats as the second forest threat. Pack 1–2,
    // very fast (0.5x movement_delay). Same eligibility as Giant Rat so
    // either can fill a Voronoi cell — the spawner picks weighted-uniform
    // (default weight 100) when the entry omits `weight:`.
    (monster: "Jackal", min_floor: 1, max_floor: 2, min_group: 1, max_group: 2),

    // Treant: very rare floor 2-3 mini-boss. weight: 5 against the
    // default 100 means it spawns ~2.4% as often as a Giant Rat / Jackal
    // entry on the same floor → most floors won't see one; when one
    // appears, it's a memorable encounter. Solo (min_group=max_group=1).
    // See assets/monsters.ron for the stat sheet.
    (monster: "Treant", min_floor: 2, max_floor: 3, min_group: 1, max_group: 1, weight: 5),
  ]
)

// ======================================================================
// LEGACY 26-FLOOR DUNGEON SPAWN TABLE (kept for reference)
// ======================================================================
//
// Restored monster entries below — uncomment and move into the `spawns:`
// list above as we re-introduce each one through the brainstorm /
// design-doc loop. Floor numbers reference the *old* 26-floor pipeline;
// re-tag for the linear forest before re-enabling.
//
//     (monster: "Sewer Rat",     min_floor: 1, max_floor: 5, min_group: 1, max_group: 3),
//     (monster: "Giant Bat",     min_floor: 1, max_floor: 3, min_group: 1, max_group: 2),
//     (monster: "Plague Rat",    min_floor: 3, max_floor: 7, min_group: 1, max_group: 2),
//     (monster: "Goblin",        min_floor: 1, max_floor: 4, min_group: 1, max_group: 3),
//     (monster: "Kobold Hoarder", min_floor: 1, max_floor: 5, min_group: 1, max_group: 2),
//     (monster: "Pit Bloat",     min_floor: 1, max_floor: 5, min_group: 1, max_group: 1),
//     (monster: "Bloat",         min_floor: 2, max_floor: 6, min_group: 1, max_group: 1),
//     (monster: "Eel",           min_floor: 1, max_floor: 10, min_group: 1, max_group: 2, spawn_on_liquid: true),
//     (monster: "Wolf",          min_floor: 4, max_floor: 7, min_group: 1, max_group: 3),
//     (monster: "Cave Bear",     min_floor: 7, max_floor: 10),
//     (monster: "Giant Spider",  min_floor: 5, max_floor: 9, min_group: 1, max_group: 2),
//     (monster: "Fire Salamander", min_floor: 5, max_floor: 9, min_group: 1, max_group: 1),
//     ... etc. The full legacy table is preserved in git history if
//     more is ever needed. Most dungeon-tier monsters (Skeletons,
//     Dragons, Constructs, Liches) are unlikely to return without a
//     re-themed pass for the forest setting.
